// spec: a `private` variable cannot have C linkage (design.md 15): its name is its file's, and C's names are the program's, so `private` inside `extern "C" { }` is an error
// found reviewing the C name of an extern "C" variable (kpp/extern_c_variable_in_library), which has no file prefix: two files' private C variables of one name would be one symbol
// error: a private declaration declares a name of its file: no namespace, import or extern "C"
extern "C"
{
  private int counter = 5;
}
int main()
{
  return counter;
}
